"Other nations have arcanophany but, as far as anyone knows, no augera; all known ones are Aiesta's."
"Aiesta's arcanophanic edge rests on the augera chained in its Spires, which no neighbour has."
"Sedhahn agents attacked Caden Dundale's convoy near Creyvlor and the Ka'atryn manor in Geldor."
"Sedhahns seem to hunt the Chosen One; at the manor they wanted him taken alive."
"Sedhahns can veil themselves in oblivion and fly unseen, raining fire and shield-piercing beams."
"The attackers' true origin is hidden even from the augera and the Demiurge; outside powers are at work."
"A Watcher, black-haired with emerald eyes, says he is of no nation Caden knows, not Aiesta nor Sedhah."
"The Watcher opposes the Fateweavers and slips past them by friendship with the augera web."
"The Watcher says the Fateweavers have not had to move like this in almost a thousand years."
"The Fateweaver who met Caden Dundale spoke with a strange, almost foreign accent."
"The augera web reaches across the Empire and a little way beyond its borders."
"Ambient arcana from outside the Empire carries no prophetic links."
"Old surveys of nations, such as The Powers That Be, lie in the Vault; public encyclopedias are edited."
"The Powers That Be: A Survey of the Nations is a translation prefaced by a past Demiurge."
"Its author seems to be an elf, reckoning ages by 'our' harvests."
"Most nations in that survey are unknown today and presumably long dead."
"The Vault keeps a proto-arcanist text in a non-Aiestan tongue, with a grammar and an encyclopedia."
"The kingdom that once averted a Prophecy did it with its combined resources, nearly ruining Aiesta."
"Ms Pearl, an agent, spent years abroad; four of her team of five died in a border field of wild arcana."
